# CloudFront Distribution

To use CloudFront, you create a **CloudFront distribution**.

A distribution defines how CloudFront should deliver content.

It contains configuration such as:

- Origin
- Cache behaviors
- Viewer protocol policy
- Allowed HTTP methods
- SSL/TLS certificate
- Cache policies
- Security settings

Conceptually:

```text
                CloudFront Distribution
                         │
          ┌──────────────┼──────────────┐
          ↓              ↓              ↓
        Origin      Cache Behavior    Security
          │              │              │
          ↓              ↓              ↓
         S3          /images/*        HTTPS
```

---

# Cache Behaviors

CloudFront allows different behaviors for different URL paths.

For example:

```text
/images/*
    ↓
S3

/api/*
    ↓
ALB
```

This allows a single CloudFront distribution to handle different types of content.

Example:

```text
example.com/images/logo.png
          ↓
       CloudFront
          ↓
          S3
```

While:

```text
example.com/api/users
          ↓
       CloudFront
          ↓
          ALB
          ↓
       Backend
```

