# CloudFront and HTTPS

CloudFront supports HTTPS for secure communication between users and CloudFront.

A typical architecture can be:

```text
User
 ↓
HTTPS
 ↓
CloudFront
 ↓
HTTPS
 ↓
Origin
```

An SSL/TLS certificate can be configured for the CloudFront distribution, commonly using **AWS Certificate Manager (ACM)**.

This allows users to securely access a domain such as:

```text
https://example.com
```

---

# CloudFront and Security

CloudFront can also work with AWS security services.

For example:

```text
User
 ↓
CloudFront
 ↓
AWS WAF
 ↓
Origin
```

**AWS WAF (Web Application Firewall)** can help protect web applications from common web attacks and unwanted traffic.

CloudFront can also help reduce direct exposure of the origin in appropriate architectures.

---

# CloudFront with AWS WAF

A common production architecture is:

```text
                 Users
                   ↓
               CloudFront
                   ↓
                  WAF
                   ↓
                  ALB
                   ↓
             EC2 / ECS / EKS
```

Here:

- CloudFront → Global content delivery
- WAF → Web traffic filtering/protection
- ALB → Application-level load balancing
- EC2/ECS/EKS → Application workloads

