# CloudFront vs S3

These services have different purposes.

### Amazon S3

Used primarily for:

```text
Object storage
```

### CloudFront

Used primarily for:

```text
Content delivery
```

They work very well together:

```text
S3
 ↓
CloudFront
 ↓
Users
```

S3 stores the content, while CloudFront distributes it efficiently.

---

# CloudFront vs ALB

They also solve different problems.

### CloudFront

```text
Global content delivery
Caching
CDN
Edge locations
```

### ALB

```text
HTTP/HTTPS load balancing
Application-level routing
Target groups
Health checks
```

They can be used together:

```text
User
 ↓
CloudFront
 ↓
ALB
 ↓
EC2/ECS/EKS
```

