# Key Takeaway

The easiest way I remember CloudFront is:

```text
CloudFront = AWS CDN
```

Its main purpose is:

> **Deliver content faster by caching and serving it from locations closer to users.**

The basic flow is:

```text
User
  ↓
CloudFront
  ↓
Edge Location
  ↓
Cache Hit → Return Content
  │
  └── Cache Miss
          ↓
        Origin
          ↓
    Get Content
          ↓
    Cache + Return
```

CloudFront is especially useful when building **globally accessible, scalable, and secure web applications** because it can work together with services such as **S3, ALB, Route 53, ACM, and AWS WAF**.